==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 4~13.33 seconds<sup>120f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 4~13.33 seconds<sup>120f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 4~13.33 seconds<sup>120f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 10~20 seconds<sup>300f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
Upgrade your [[Worker Cat]] to max level. When the enemies come near your base, send out a few [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]]. In the meantime, wait for your money to build up. When B.B.Bunny appears, start spamming [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Axe Cats]]. At this point, your wallet should be full, so send out all of your [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] at once. When the base is hit and Kang Roo appears, there is no need to worry - Kang Roo can only hit one cat at a time, so if you spam [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cats]] and Tank Cats you can use almost any attacker to beat her, whether it be [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]], or a spam of [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cats]]. A [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cat]] or two can speed up the level.

